For the explicitly requested deep review, examine cross-file invariants and architectural assumptions affected by the change. Attack the premise of the change: question unstated assumptions rather than only checking local syntax. Select relevant risks: public API compatibility, concurrency and ordering, partial failure, migration and rollback, or trust boundaries. Use `security-audit` for security analysis.

Support findings with concrete edge cases or adversarial scenarios. When the harness supports multi-model delegation, stress-test contested designs across model families to eliminate single-model blind spots. Distinguish scenarios reasoned through from tests actually executed. End with a merge verdict (safe to merge, merge with fixes, or do not merge) and a brief justification that accounts for material coverage gaps.
